    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I think I just found something huge. I was looking through some old corporate archives I managed to access, and I found a memo from five years ago that explicitly mentions \"contingency protocols for the dormant trust assets\" in direct relation to my family name. It’s clearly a blueprint for how they planned to bypass my claim once I came of age. Does this confirm that they've had this contingency plan in place for years? And how can I use this specific memo to prove that their current management isn't just incompetent, but is actually acting under a premeditated plan to disenfranchise me?",
